  "cover_text": "Mahatma Gandhi1 once said, “The world provides enough for the needs of nations, but not enough for individual desires.”\nAlthough the idea of right and wrong is at the heart of most discussions in the public domain over the last few days, it is so important to the individual, though not always wondered over. There are many kinds of importance, senses of being told to do or what it is.\n- It’s true that not all actions are based on right and wrong.\n- It doesn’t mean there is one right answer to each and every situation, choice, or answer.\nIn his time, Gandhi was on the peripheriesof history. At the height of his life, when he began",
